# Calls the raster-math check ignores. A rule is `METHOD PATH` or `METHOD() PATH`.
# PATH is a repo-relative file, or `*` for every file under vendor/.
# `METHOD()` matches only a call with no arguments. `f32` and `f64` hypot and atan2
# take an argument, so a zero-argument call is some other method (kurbo's Vec2).
# `sqrt` is not listed: clippy.toml allows it (correctly rounded on every platform).

# Exponentiation by squaring in Rust core, the same bits on every platform, not a
# platform libm. clippy.toml bans powi in this repository's own crates; `math` has
# no powi wrapper, and the vendored crates keep the upstream calls.
powi *

# Vec2::hypot is hypot2().sqrt(). Vec2::atan2 is y.p_atan2(x). See kurbo vec2.rs.
hypot() *
atan2() *

# f32x8::powf in wide/f32x8_t.rs is a bit-trick approximation. These are its calls
# (gradient and colour-space stages). A sin or cos in this file still fails the check.
powf vendor/tiny-skia/src/pipeline/highp.rs
